<algorithm id="fig001">
<meta>
<id>365.2</id>
<supertype>AbCd</supertype>
<last_update>2007-09-13</last_update>
</meta>
<title>Cushing's Syndrome: Diagnosis of Hypercortisolism.</title>
<graphic href="eee0121-w001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Clinical suspicion for Cushing's syndrome (CS)? Select initial diagnostic test.</label>
<path target="cell-2">11 PM salivary cortisol</path>
<path target="cell-3">Overnight 1-mg dexamethasone suppression test</path>
<path target="cell-4">24-hour urinary free cortisol</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Result? (Normal &lt;0.11 &#x03BC;g&#x002F;dL)</label>
<path target="cell-5">Over 0.25 µg/dL</path>
<path target="cell-7">Under 0.11 µg/dL</path>
<path target="cell-6">0.11–0.25 µg/dL</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>CS very likely.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-6">
<label>Order low-dose dexamethasone suppression test (2-d 2-mg test). Plasma cortisol &#x003E;1.8 &#x03BC;g&#x002F;dL and plasma dexamethasone 2.0-6.5 ng&#x002F;mL?</label>
<path target="cell-8">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-9">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>CS confirmed.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-9">
<label>CS ruled out.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>CS unlikely.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Result? (Normal &lt;1.8 &#x03BC;g&#x002F;dL)</label>
<path target="cell-7">Under 1.8 µg/dL</path>
<path target="cell-6">Over 1.8 µg/dL</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Result? (Normal 20-100 &#x03BC;g&#x002F;dL)</label>
<path target="cell-7">20–100 µg/dL</path>
<path target="cell-10">100–400 µg/dL</path>
<path target="cell-6">Over 400 µg/dL</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-10">
<label>CS very likely.</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>.</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
<algorithm id="fig002">
<meta>
<id>365.3</id>
<supertype>AbCd</supertype>
<last_update>2007-09-13</last_update>
</meta>
<title>Cushing's Syndrome: Determining the Cause of Hypercortisolism.</title>
<graphic href="eee0121-w002.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-11">
<label>Biochemical confirmation of CS. Order ACTH level.</label>
<path target="cell-12">ACTH 5 pg/mL or more (ACTH-dependent)</path>
<path target="cell-14">ACTH under 5 pg/mL (ACTH-independent)</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-12">
<label>Two options: (1) High-dose dexamethasone suppression test. Give 8 mg by mouth overnight or 2 mg every 6 h for 48 h; &#x003E;50&#x0025; serum cortisol suppression? (2) CRH stimulation test. &#x003E;20&#x0025; increase above basal serum cortisol post-CRH or &#x003E;35&#x0025; increase above basal serum ACTH post-CRH?</label>
<path target="cell-15">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-13">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-15">
<label>Cushing's disease.</label>
<path target="cell-18"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-18">
<label>MRI scan pituitary, surgery for operable tumor.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-16">
<label>BIPSS with CRH. Gradient present (BIPSS to peripheral ACTH ratio &#x003E;2 in the basal state and&#x002F;or &#x003E;3 after CRH)?</label>
<path target="cell-18">Gradient</path>
<path target="cell-19">No gradient</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-19">
<label>CT&#x002F;MRI (neck&#x002F;chest&#x002F;abdomen&#x002F;pelvis) or octreotide scan.</label>
<path target="cell-20">Ectopic source localized</path>
<path target="cell-21">Not localized</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-20">
<label>Surgery for operable tumor.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-21">
<label>Follow-up and re-image.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-17">
<label>Ectopic ACTH syndrome.</label>
<path target="cell-19"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-13">
<label>High suspicion for ectopic ACTH syndrome?</label>
<path target="cell-17">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-16">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-14">
<label>Order CT or MRI of adrenals. Suspect primary adrenal disorders: Adrenal adenoma or carcinoma, macronodular or micronodular hyperplasia.</label>
</cell>
</algorithm>
</algorithms>
